        "thinking": "`getOrExtractUiParserSource` first checks `uiParserCache` (in-memory), then `getAdapterPluginByType(adapterType)` (reads JSON store from FS, falls back to empty). For built-in adapters, there's no record in the external plugin store, so `getAdapterPluginByType` returns `undefined`. This means `getOrExtractUiParserSource` returns `undefined` for built-in adapters.\n\nFor the `GET /api/adapters/:type/ui-parser.js` handler, it would return 404 for built-in adapters. \n\nThat's acceptable. The `config-schema` endpoint calls `findActiveServerAdapter(type)` to get the adapter from memory, then retrieves its config schema directly from the module, which works fine for built-in adapters. So adding the adapter routes would give us working endpoints for config-schema and ui-parser.js (404 for built-ins), plus the PATCH endpoint for updates.\n\nThe mutation operations like install, delete, and reload would fail at runtime since they depend on filesystem access, but that's expected in this environment. The read operations are what matter for the UI to function. Since `adapterRoutes()` already wraps everything with `expressHandler`, the existing extraction logic in `route-registry.ts` should pick them all up correctly. I'll add `adapterRoutes` to the registry.",
